# Headers for the app's site on Cloudflare, which reads this file from the
# build and doesn't serve it. What only a header can say: no other site may
# frame the app (the rest of its security policy is the meta tag in
# index.html), and a file under /assets/, whose name changes with what's in
# it, can be kept for a year. index.html and sw.js keep Cloudflare's default,
# checked again on every visit, so an update reaches everyone.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
